        <p>EARLESTOWN V. Sr. HELENS RECS.—This match WAS played at Earlestown on Saturday before 1,000 specta- tors. Result :—St. Helens Recreation, three goals; Earlestown: one.</p>
        <p>At Omagh. county Tyrone, on Tuesday, a farm labourer named Joseph Moan was remanded charged with the murder of a married woman named Rose M'Cann, near Trillick, on November 20th last. The body of the deceased woman, which was found in a bog hole, bore evidence of shocking ill-treatment and violence. At thelime of the occurrence she was returning „from marketing, and in addition to the indications of ill- ii suage, the medical evidence showed that she had also h e en outraged. ,There Is Stecturlty ls A stOOthIFL tootila</p>
