      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-12-12_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
        <head>comnaunical</head>
        <p>comnaunical</p>
        <p>HIS SKIN WENT YELLOW. Through Liver Disorder and Indigestion. BILE BEANS EFFECTS A RADICAL CURE. A Glass-workers' Striking Testimony.</p>
        <p>The account of the wonderful cure by Chas. Forde's Bile Beans of a glass-worker, named Patrick Hynes, of 154, Back West&amp;ld-street, St. Helens, is full of interest- ing facts for Warrington workers. Mr. Hynes is em- ployed at the works of Messrs. Dixon. Nuttall and Co., and his work there was responsible for a com- plete breakdown in his health. Here are the details of his case as he told them to a "St. Helena Reporter" representative. Said he :- 1 "About six years* ago, I suffered from liver com- plaint, and was temporarily relieved by a doctor of this town. Then four years ago I began to be very bad again. My skin commenced to look very yellow, and I got so weak that all I seemed fit for was to lie in bed. Then I commenced to suffer from indigestion, and the pains I endured seemed to affect All parts of my body. My head ached very much, and my left arm was so painful that I could scarcely lift it. " I had the advice of several doctors, but without effect; they could not tell what was the matter with me. and the last one I saw said that I had left matters too long, and that I should NEVER BE WELL AGAIN. At this time I appeared to be losing the power of using my legs. I had to remain indoors, and I could scarcely , crawl along the floor of the kitchen. I "One Saturday, hardly knowing what to do with my- self. I happened to see an account of the wonderful qualities of Chas. Forde's Bile Beans, and I determined to give them a trial. I purchased a box from Mr Wall- bridge chemist, of Liverpool-road, and after taking the Beans I felt so much better that I sent for some more. "By the time I had taken a thorough course, my com- plexion had completely changed to a-healthy colour. I am now quite restored to health. I can digest my food as well as if I was a young man of twenty-two ; I no longer suffer from liver complaint or weakness, and all these good results have been attained,by the use of Bile Beans. Indeed, I consider that I should have been in my grave now had it not been for them." . _</p>
        <p>Forde's Bile Beans for Biliousness which accom- panied the above cure are purely vegetable in composi- tion and their excellence has been so well proved that many eminent doctors are now prescribing them largely. They are a certain cure for indigestion, congestion of the liver, headache, pains in the chest, loins or back, neuralgia, general weakness, dizziness, biliousness, flatulence, defective secretion of bile, wasting affections, female irregularities, colds, chill, rheumatism, influenza, skin eruptions, pimples, and the host of ailments having a common origin in impurity of the blood, a general congestion of the system, and loss of vital force. Obtainable from all chemists, or post free from the Bile Bean Manufacturing Co.. Red Cross-street, London, 8.C., upon receipt of prices. Is. lid. or 2s. 9d. per box (2a. 9d, boe contains 3 times Is. lid. size). Bile Beans are sold only in sealed boxes; never loose.</p>
